WEBVTT

00:08:59.302 --> 00:09:01.938
and I have people in my life
that love me for who I am

00:09:01.971 --> 00:09:03.406
and not what I do.

00:09:05.475 --> 00:09:08.078
You can take a breather so I can too.”

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:12.382
As you're ready,

00:09:12.415 --> 00:09:14.284
just gently opening your eyes back up

00:09:14.317 --> 00:09:16.586
and coming back into the room with me.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:18.888
Welcome back.

00:09:20.857 --> 00:09:22.625
So part of that reflection activity

00:09:22.659 --> 00:09:25.829
is an example of what
we would technically call

00:09:25.862 --> 00:09:28.131
identifying our cognitive schemas.

00:09:28.832 --> 00:09:32.702
Our cognitive schemas are essentially
how our brain forms